{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "```python\n\"\"\"\nProvides find_Rotations(s) to find the minimum positive cyclic rotation.\nIncludes _rotate(s, k) as a helper for string rotation.\n\"\"\"\n\ndef _rotate(s: str, k: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the left cyclic rotation of string s by k characters.\n    It returns the string s[k:] + s[:k].\n    \"\"\"\n    return s[k:] + s[:k]\n\ndef find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the minimum positive integer k (> 0) such that rotating s by k yields s.\n    If no such k in 1..len(s)-1 is found, it returns len(s).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # Iterate k from 1 to n-1.\n    # If n is 0 or 1, range(1, n) will be empty, and n will be returned.\n    for k in range(1, n):\n        rotated_s = _rotate(s, k)\n        if rotated_s == s:\n            return k\n    \n    # If no k in 1..len(s)-1 matched, return len(s).\n    return n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "```python\n# src/find_rotations.py\n# Implementation of find_Rotations(s: str) per SRS; no external dependencies.\n\ndef _left_rotate(s: str, k: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Helper to perform a left rotation on string s by k positions.\"\"\"\n    return s[k:] + s[:k]\n\ndef find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the smallest positive left-rotation count k for string s.\"\"\"\n    if len(s) == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    n = len(s)\n    for k in range(1, n):\n        rotated = _left_rotate(s, k)\n        if rotated == s:\n            return k\n    \n    return n\n\n```\n```python\n# tests/test_find_rotations.py\nfrom src.find_rotations import find_Rotations\n\ndef run_assertion() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Executes the required assertion and prints a success message.\"\"\"\n    print(f\"Running assertion: assert find_Rotations('aaaa') == 1\")\n    assert find_Rotations(\"aaaa\") == 1\n    print(\"Assertion passed: find_Rotations('aaaa') == 1\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    run_assertion()\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(input_str: str, ch: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrence of a specified character from an input string.\"\"\"\n    first_index = input_str.find(ch)\n    last_index = input_str.rfind(ch)\n\n    if first_index == -1:  # Character not found, return original string\n        return input_str\n    \n    if first_index == last_index:  # Only one occurrence\n        return input_str[:first_index] + input_str[first_index+1:]\n    else:  # Distinct first and last occurrences\n        # Remove the character at the last_index first to avoid index shifting for the first_index\n        temp = input_str[:last_index] + input_str[last_index+1:]\n        # Remove the character at the first_index from the temporary string\n        result = temp[:first_index] + temp[first_index+1:]\n        return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(s: str, c: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrence of character c from string s.\n    Returns the modified string or the original if c is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    first_index = s.find(c)\n\n    if first_index == -1:\n        return s\n\n    last_index = s.rfind(c)\n\n    if first_index == last_index:\n        # Only one occurrence of c\n        return s[:first_index] + s[first_index+1:]\n    else:\n        # Multiple occurrences: remove both first and last\n        return s[:first_index] + s[first_index+1:last_index] + s[last_index+1:]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_matrix(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a matrix (list of lists) by the ascending sum of its rows.\n    Returns a new matrix without modifying the input.\n    \"\"\"\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    # Create tuples of (row_sum, original_row_reference) for each row.\n    for row in matrix:\n        rows_with_sums.append((sum(row), row))\n\n    # Sort these tuples primarily by the row_sum. Python's sorted() is stable.\n    sorted_rows_with_sums = sorted(rows_with_sums, key=lambda item: item[0])\n\n    # Construct the new matrix using the sorted row references.\n    result_matrix = [row_content for _, row_content in sorted_rows_with_sums]\n\n    return result_matrix\n```"}
