{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Monotonic(array: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a list is monotonic (non-decreasing or non-increasing).\n    Adjacent equal elements are considered valid for monotonicity.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_non_decreasing = True\n    is_non_increasing = True\n\n    for i in range(len(array) - 1):\n        if array[i] > array[i+1]:\n            is_non_decreasing = False\n        if array[i] < array[i+1]:\n            is_non_increasing = False\n\n        if not is_non_decreasing and not is_non_increasing:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "```python\nclass Element:\n    \"\"\"Wraps a value, providing custom equality semantics.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self.value = value\n\n    def equals(self, other) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Compares wrapped value or raw value for equality.\"\"\"\n        # Design specifies: if other is Element compare self.value == other.value else compare self.value == other\n        # Using isinstance to robustly check if 'other' is an Element instance for value comparison.\n        if isinstance(other, Element):\n            return self.value == other.value\n        return self.value == other\n\n\ndef _compare_elements(a, b) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Compares two elements based on design's equality semantics.\"\"\"\n    # Design: Use Element.equals(other) when elements are Element instances; otherwise use native equality (==).\n    if isinstance(a, Element) and isinstance(b, Element):\n        return a.equals(b)\n    elif isinstance(a, Element):  # If only 'a' is Element, try a.equals(b) for comparison.\n        return a.equals(b)\n    elif isinstance(b, Element):  # If only 'b' is Element, try b.equals(a) for symmetry.\n        return b.equals(a)\n    else:  # Neither is an Element instance, use native equality.\n        return a == b\n\n\ndef is_sublist(main_list, sub_list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if sub_list appears in main_list as a contiguous subsequence.\n    Does not modify input lists and uses element equality semantics.\n    \"\"\"\n    m = len(main_list)\n    n = len(sub_list)\n\n    # FR4: If len(sub_list) > len(main_list) return False.\n    if n > m:\n        return False\n\n    # Empty-sublist semantics: Treat empty sub_list as True (documented design choice).\n    if n == 0:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate through possible starting positions in main_list.\n    for i in range(m - n + 1):\n        match = True\n        # Compare corresponding elements of the candidate sublist.\n        for j in range(n):\n            # FR6: Compare elements using equality semantics provided by _compare_elements.\n            if not _compare_elements(main_list[i + j], sub_list[j]):\n                match = False\n                break\n        if match:\n            return True\n\n    return False\n```"}
