{"task_id": "Mbpp/90", "solution": "```python\n# src/len_log.py\n\ndef _validate_input(words: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates the input to be a list of strings.\n    Raises ValueError if the input is not a list or contains non-string elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(words, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    for word in words:\n        if not isinstance(word, str):\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements in the list must be strings.\")\n    return True\n\ndef _find_longest_length(words: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the length of the longest string in the given list.\n    Returns 0 if the list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not words:\n        return 0\n    longest = 0\n    for word in words:\n        longest = max(longest, len(word))\n    return longest\n\ndef len_log(words: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest string in a list of strings.\n    Validates input and raises ValueError for invalid types.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(words)\n    return _find_longest_length(words)\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_len_log.py\n\nimport sys\nimport os\n\n# Adjust the Python path to allow importing from the 'src' directory\ncurrent_dir = os.path.dirname(__file__)\nparent_dir = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(current_dir, '..'))\nsrc_dir = os.path.join(parent_dir, 'src')\nsys.path.insert(0, src_dir)\n\nfrom len_log import len_log\n\ndef test_len_log_example() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Tests the len_log function with the specific example from the SRS.\"\"\"\n    assert len_log(['python','PHP','bigdata']) == 7\n```"}
