{"task_id": "Mbpp/145", "solution": "```python\n# src/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nPackage marker for src.\nRe-exports the public API function max_Abs_Diff.\n\"\"\"\n__all__ = [\"max_Abs_Diff\"]\nfrom .max_abs_diff import max_Abs_Diff\n\n```python\n# src/max_abs_diff.py\n\"\"\"\nThis module provides the max_Abs_Diff function to compute the maximum absolute\ndifference between any two numeric elements in an array, adhering to O(n) time\nand O(1) space complexity. It includes helper functions for input validation\nand min/max computation.\n\"\"\"\n\ndef validate_input(input: object) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates input type and content, raising errors for invalid cases.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input, (list, tuple)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list or tuple.\")\n    \n    if len(input) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must contain at least two elements.\")\n        \n    for element in input:\n        if not isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the input must be numeric (int or float).\")\n    return True\n\ndef compute_min_max(input: list|tuple) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Computes the minimum and maximum values in a numeric array in a single pass.\"\"\"\n    min_value = float(input[0])\n    max_value = float(input[0])\n    # Iterate from the second element as the first element initialized min_value and max_value.\n    for element in input[1:]:\n        numeric_element = float(element)\n        if numeric_element < min_value:\n            min_value = numeric_element\n        if numeric_element > max_value:\n            max_value = numeric_element\n    return min_value, max_value\n\ndef max_Abs_Diff(input: list|tuple) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Computes the maximum absolute difference between any two numeric elements of an input array.\"\"\"\n    validate_input(input)\n    min_val, max_val = compute_min_max(input)\n    return float(max_val - min_val)\n\n```python\n# tests/test_max_abs_diff.py\n\"\"\"\nUnit