{"task_id": "Mbpp/227", "solution": "```python\n# src/min_of_three.py\n\n\"\"\"\nModule for finding the minimum of three numbers.\nIt provides a single function: min_of_three.\n\"\"\"\n\ndef min_of_three(a: float, b: float, c: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the smallest value among three numeric arguments.\n    Compares a, b, and c to determine the minimum.\n    \"\"\"\n    return min(a, b, c)\n\n```\n```python\n# tests/test_min_of_three.py\n\n\"\"\"\nUnit tests for the min_of_three function.\nVerifies the function returns the expected minimum value.\n\"\"\"\nfrom src.min_of_three import min_of_three\n\ndef test_min_of_three():\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests min_of_three with specific integer inputs.\n    Asserts that min_of_three(10, 20, 0) correctly returns 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert min_of_three(10, 20, 0) == 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/227", "solution": "```python\n# src/min_of_three.py\n\nclass NumericInput:\n    \"\"\"Represents and validates a single numeric input.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not an int or float.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        if not isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a numeric value (int or float).\")\n        self.value = value\n        self.type_name = type(value).__name__\n\nclass Result:\n    \"\"\"Represents the numeric result value.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self.value = value\n\nclass MinOfThree:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the computation logic to find the smallest of three numbers.\n    This class is stateless and provides the core algorithm.\"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def min_of_three(a: float | int, b: float | int, c: float | int) -> float | int:\n        \"\"\"Compares three numeric values and returns the minimum among them.\"\"\"\n        return min(a, b, c)\n\ndef min_of_three(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"Public API to compute and return the smallest of three numeric inputs.\n    Validates inputs and delegates computation to the MinOfThree class.\"\"\"\n    # Validate inputs through NumericInput objects, which raise TypeError on invalid types.\n    numeric_a = NumericInput(a).value\n    numeric_b = NumericInput(b).value\n    numeric_c = NumericInput(c).value\n\n    # Delegate the actual computation to the MinOfThree domain class.\n    smallest_value = MinOfThree.min_of_three(numeric_a, numeric_b, numeric_c)\n\n    # Wrap the result in a Result object and return its value.\n    return Result(smallest_value).value\n\n```\n```python\n# tests/test_min_of_three.py\n\nfrom src.min_of_three import min_of_three, MinOfThree, NumericInput, Result\n\nclass TestCase:\n    \"\"\"Represents a single test case for the min_of_three function.\n    It holds input values, expected output, and a name for descriptive reporting.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, input_values: tuple, expected_output: float | int, name: str = \"Unnamed Test\"):\n        self.input_values = input_values\n        self.expected_output = expected_output\n        self.name = name\n\n    def run(self):\n        \"\"\"Executes the test case by calling min_of_three and asserting the result.\n        Raises AssertionError if the actual output does not match the expected output.\"\"\"\n        a, b, c = self.input_values\n        print(f\"Running test: '{self.name}' with inputs {self.input_values}...\")\n        \n        actual_output = min_of_three(a, b, c)\n\n        if actual_output == self.expected_output:\n            print(f\"  PASS: Expected {self.expected_output}, got {actual_output}\")\n        else:\n            raise AssertionError(\n                f\"  FAIL: For inputs {self.input_values}, expected {self.expected_output}, but got {actual_output}\"\n            )\n\ndef run_all_tests():\n    \"\"\"Entry point for running all defined test cases.\n    Currently runs the canonical test specified in the design.\"\"\"\n    print(\"--- Starting All Tests ---\")\n    \n    # Canonical test case from the design specification.\n    canonical_test = TestCase((10, 20, 0), expected_output=0, name=\"Canonical Test (10,20,0)==0\")\n    canonical_test.run()\n    \n    print(\"--- All Tests Completed ---\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    run_all_tests()\n```"}
