{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef compute_magnitude(real: float, imag: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Computes the magnitude (r) from real and imaginary parts.\"\"\"\n    return math.sqrt(real**2 + imag**2)\n\ndef compute_angle(real: float, imag: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Computes the angle (theta) in radians from real and imaginary parts.\"\"\"\n    return math.atan2(imag, real)\n\ndef convert(z) -> (float, float):\n    \"\"\"Converts a complex number or real numeric value to polar coordinates (r, theta).\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(z, complex):\n        re = z.real\n        im = z.imag\n    else:\n        re = float(z)\n        im = 0.0\n    \n    r = compute_magnitude(re, im)\n    theta = compute_angle(re, im)\n    \n    return (r, theta)\n```"}
