_dog_age = dog_age(12)\n        self.assertEqual(expected_dog_age, actual_dog_age)\n        print(f\"Test dog_age(12) passed: {actual_dog_age}\")\n\n    def assertEqual(self, expected: int, actual: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Asserts that two integer values are equal.\n        Raises AssertionError if values differ.\"\"\"\n        if expected != actual:\n            raise AssertionError(f\"Assertion failed: expected={expected}, actual={actual}\")\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/main.py\nfrom src.test_suite import TestSuite\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the application.\n    It triggers the execution of the TestSuite.\"\"\"\n    TestSuite().run()\n```"}
