{"task_id": "Mbpp/269", "solution": "```python\n# src/ascii_value.py\n\n# Domain/value classes\nclass Character:\n    \"\"\"Value object representing input; holds value (str) and provides length().\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: str):\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"Character value must be a string.\")\n        self.value = value\n\n    def length(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the length of the encapsulated character string.\"\"\"\n        return len(self.value)\n\nclass AsciiCode:\n    \"\"\"Value object holding the result integer ASCII code.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        if not isinstance(value, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"AsciiCode value must be an integer.\")\n        self.value = value\n\n# Internal helpers\ndef _validate_single_character(char: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Raises ValueError if char is not a single-character string.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(char, str) or len(char) != 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"input must be a single character\")\n\ndef _map_char_to_ascii(char: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Returns ord(char) if within 0..127; else raises ValueError.\"\"\"\n    code = ord(char)\n    if not (0 <= code <= 127):\n        raise ValueError(\"character outside ASCII range\")\n    return code\n\nclass AsciiFunction:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates ascii_value operation; provides method form ascii_value(char) -> int.\"\"\"\n    def ascii_value(self, char: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Implements the ascii_value logic using internal helpers.\"\"\"\n        _validate_single_character(char)\n        code = _map_char_to_ascii(char)\n        return code\n\n# Public API\ndef ascii_value(char: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Public API: ascii_value(char) -> int\n    Validates char is a single-character string, maps to ASCII code, and returns int.\n    Raises ValueError on invalid input or if character is outside ASCII range.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_single_character(char)\n    code = _map_char_to_ascii(char)\n    return code\n```"}
