{"task_id": "Mbpp/270", "solution": "```python\n\"\"\"\nThis module provides the sum_even_and_even_index function, which sums even-valued elements at even indices.\nIt is a minimal Python implementation as per design specifications.\n\"\"\"\n\ndef _is_even(value: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a numeric value is an even integer.\n    Assumes `value` is an integer as per design constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n    return value % 2 == 0\n\ndef sum_even_and_even_index(input_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of elements that are both even-valued and located at even indices (0-based).\n    Returns 0 if no elements match the criteria.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i, value in enumerate(input_list):\n        # Include element if its index is even and its value is even.\n        if i % 2 == 0 and _is_even(value):\n            total_sum += value\n    return total_sum\n```"}
