{"task_id": "Mbpp/281", "solution": "```python\ndef all_unique(list_: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if all elements in the given list are unique.\n    Uses an O(n) set-based approach with a fallback to O(n^2) for unhashable elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_:\n        return True\n\n    seen = set()\n    try:\n        for item in list_:\n            if item in seen:\n                return False\n            seen.add(item)\n        return True\n    except TypeError:\n        # Fallback for unhashable elements if set operations fail\n        # This compares elements pairwise using Python's == semantics.\n        n = len(list_)\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                if list_[i] == list_[j]:\n                    return False\n        return True\n```"}
