{"task_id": "Mbpp/290", "solution": "```python\ndef max_length(list_of_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the inner list with the maximum length in a list of lists.\n    Returns a tuple (max_len, max_list) where max_len is the length\n    and max_list is the first encountered list with that length.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_len_found = 0\n    longest_list_found = []\n\n    for inner_list in list_of_lists:\n        current_len = len(inner_list)\n        if current_len > max_len_found:\n            max_len_found = current_len\n            longest_list_found = inner_list\n\n    return (max_len_found, longest_list_found)\n```\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom src.max_length import max_length\n\ndef test_example_assertion():\n    \"\"\"Runs the SRS-provided example assertion to verify the max_length function.\"\"\"\n    input_data = [[0], [1, 3], [5, 7], [9, 11], [13, 15, 17]]\n    expected_output = (3, [13, 15, 17])\n    actual_output = max_length(input_data)\n    assert actual_output == expected_output, \\\n        f\"Verification failed: Expected {expected_output}, but got {actual_output}\"\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        test_example_assertion()\n        print(\"PASS\")\n        sys.exit(0)\n    except AssertionError as e:\n        print(f\"FAIL: {e}\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/287", "solution": "def square_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of squares of the first n even natural numbers.\n    Assumes n is a non-negative integer as per critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The sum is 4 * sum_{k=1..n} k^2, where sum_{k=1..n} k^2 = n(n+1)(2n+1)/6.\n    # This simplifies to 2 * n * (n + 1) * (2 * n + 1) // 3.\n    return (2 * n * (n + 1) * (2 * n + 1)) // 3"}
