{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(elements: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of integers from the input list whose product is maximal.\n    Assumes valid input: a list of at least two integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(elements)\n    max_prod = float('-inf')\n    best_pair = (None, None)\n\n    # Iterate through all distinct pairs (i, j) where i < j.\n    # The first-occurring pair with the maximal product is preferred for ties.\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            current_product = elements[i] * elements[j]\n            if current_product > max_prod:\n                max_prod = current_product\n                best_pair = (elements[i], elements[j])\n\n    return best_pair"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/418", "solution": "def Find_Max(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the element in a list with the maximum length.\n    If multiple elements share the maximum length, the first encountered one is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return None\n\n    max_element = input_list[0]\n    max_len = len(input_list[0])\n\n    for element in input_list:\n        current_len = len(element)\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            max_element = element\n    return max_element"}
