{"task_id": "Mbpp/422", "solution": "```python\nclass CubeCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Computes the sum of cubes for the first n natural numbers.\n    It calculates sum(k**3) for k from 1 to n.\"\"\"\n    def sum_of_cubes(self, n: int) -> int:\n        return sum(k**3 for k in range(1, n + 1))\n\nclass AverageCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Computes the average of a given sum over n.\n    It returns a float value, even for integer averages.\"\"\"\n    def compute_average(self, sum_val: int, n: int) -> float:\n        return sum_val / n\n\ndef find_Average_Of_Cube(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the average of the cubes of the first n natural numbers.\n    It orchestrates cube summation and average computation.\"\"\"\n    total = CubeCalculator().sum_of_cubes(n)\n    return AverageCalculator().compute_average(total, n)\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/422", "solution": "```python\n# src/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nPackage marker for src.\n\"\"\"\n```\n\n```python\n# src/find_average_of_cube.py\n\"\"\"\nA module to find the average of cubes of first n natural numbers.\nIt includes a public function and internal helpers for validation, generation,\ncubing, aggregation, and average computation.\n\"\"\"\n\ndef _validate_input(n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates the input 'n'.\n    Raises TypeError if n is not an integer, or ValueError if n is less than 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be greater than or equal to 1.\")\n\ndef _generate_sequence(n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a list of natural numbers from 1 to n.\n    \"\"\"\n    return list(range(1, n + 1))\n\ndef _cube(x: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the cube of a given integer x.\n    \"\"\"\n    return x ** 3\n\ndef _sum_values(values: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of a list of integer values.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(values)\n\ndef _compute_average(sum_value: int, count: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the average of a sum over a count, ensuring a float result.\n    \"\"\"\n    return float(sum_value) / float(count)\n\ndef find_Average_Of_Cube(n) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the average of the cubes of the first n natural numbers.\n    This public API validates input, computes cubes, sums them, and returns their average.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(n)\n    \n    numbers = _generate_sequence(n)\n    cubes = [_cube(x) for x in numbers]\n    total_sum_of_cubes = _sum_values(cubes)\n    \n    return _compute_average(total_sum_of_cubes, n)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_find_average_of_cube.py\n\"\"\"\nTest script for the find_Average_Of_Cube function.\nContains the required acceptance assertion for the system.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom src.find_average_of_cube import find_Average_Of_Cube\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Executes the acceptance test for find_Average_Of_Cube.\n    Asserts that find_Average_Of_Cube(2) returns 4.5.\n    \"\"\"\n    expected_result = 4.5\n    actual_result = find_Average_Of_Cube(2)\n    assert actual_result == expected_result, f\"Test failed: Expected {expected_result}, got {actual_result}\"\n    print(f\"Acceptance test passed: find_Average_Of_Cube(2) == {actual_result}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```"}
