{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "```python\n\"\"\"\ndiff_even_odd(input_list: list[int]) -> int\n\nCompute the difference between the first even and the first odd number in input_list.\n\nParameters:\n- input_list (list[int]): an ordered list of integers to scan. The function does not modify this list.\n\nReturns:\n- int: the arithmetic result (first_even - first_odd), where first_even is the first element encountered (left-to-right) with value % 2 == 0 and first_odd is the first element encountered (left-to-right) with value % 2 != 0.\n\nError behavior:\n- If input_list does not contain at least one even and at least one odd integer, the function raises ValueError with a descriptive message (e.g., \"input_list must contain at least one even and one odd integer\"). This represents the explicit error state required by the SRS.\n\nComplexity:\n- Time: O(n) where n == len(input_list). The implementation performs a single left-to-right scan and stops early when both values are found.\n- Space: O(1) additional memory (only a fixed number of local variables used; no auxiliary collections proportional to input size).\n\nNotes:\n- The function is pure: it does not mutate input_list or any external state.\n- Example (from SRS): assert diff_even_odd([1,3,5,7,4,1,6,8]) == 3\n\"\"\"\ndef diff_even_odd(input_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n\n    for x in input_list:\n        if first_even is None and x % 2 == 0:\n            first_even = x\n        if first_odd is None and x % 2 != 0:\n            first_odd = x\n        \n        # Exit early if both first_even and first_odd have been found.\n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n    \n    if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n        return first_even - first_odd\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(\"input_list must contain at least one even and one odd integer\")\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "```python\n# src/integer_list.py\nfrom typing import List, Iterator\n\nclass IntegerList:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates an ordered integer sequence and provides methods for access.\n    Supports left-to-right scanning with an iterator.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, items: List[int]) -> None:\n        self.items = items\n\n    def length(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the number of items in the list.\"\"\"\n        return len(self.items)\n\n    def get(self, index: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the item at the specified index.\"\"\"\n        return self.items[index]\n\n    def iterator(self) -> Iterator[int]:\n        \"\"\"Returns an iterator for the items in the list.\"\"\"\n        return iter(self.items)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/number_finder.py\nfrom src.integer_list import IntegerList\n\nclass NumberFinder:\n    \"\"\"\n    Stateless service to find the first odd or even integer in an IntegerList.\n    Scans the list left-to-right.\n    \"\"\"\n    def find_first_odd(self, list: IntegerList) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Iterates left-to-right to find and return the first odd integer.\n        Raises LookupError if no odd integer is found.\n        \"\"\"\n        for element in list.iterator():\n            if element % 2 != 0:\n                return element\n        raise LookupError('No odd integer found')\n\n    def find_first_even(self, list: IntegerList) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Iterates left-to-right to find and return the first even integer.\n        Raises LookupError if no even integer is found.\n        \"\"\"\n        for element in list.iterator():\n            if element % 2 == 0:\n                return element\n        raise LookupError('No even integer found')\n\n```\n```python\n# src/result.py\nclass Result:\n    \"\"\"\n    A simple container for a computed integer value.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: int) -> None:\n        self.value = value\n\n```\n```python\n# src/diff_even_odd.py\nfrom typing import List\nfrom src.integer_list import IntegerList\nfrom src.number_finder import NumberFinder\nfrom src.result import Result  # Imported as per design for clarity\n\ndef diff_even_odd(list: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first even and first odd integers in a list and returns their difference.\n    Propagates LookupError if no odd or even number is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    wrapper = IntegerList(list)\n    finder = NumberFinder()\n    \n    first_odd = finder.find_first_odd(wrapper)\n    first_even = finder.find_first_even(wrapper)\n    \n    result_value = first_even - first_odd\n    \n    # As per design, a Result object is produced, even if its value is then directly returned.\n    _ = Result(result_value) \n    \n    return result_value\n\n```\n```python\n# src/main.py\nfrom typing import List\nfrom src.diff_even_odd import diff_even_odd\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Example runner demonstrating the usage of diff_even_odd.\n    Prints the result or any encountered error.\n    \"\"\"\n    example_list: List[int] = [1, 3, 5, 7, 4, 1, 6, 8]\n    print(f\"Input list: {example_list}\")\n    try:\n        difference = diff_even_odd(example_list)\n        print(f\"Difference (first_even - first_odd): {difference}\") # Expected: 3\n    except LookupError as e:\n        print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n\n    example_list_no_odd: List[int] = [2, 4, 6]\n    print(f\"\\nInput list: {example_list_no_odd}\")\n    try:\n        difference = diff_even_odd(example_list_no_odd)\n        print(f\"Difference (first_even - first_odd): {difference}\")\n    except LookupError as e:\n        print(f\"Error: {e}\") # Expected: No odd integer found\n\n    example_list_no_even: List[int] = [1, 3, 5]\n    print(f\"\\nInput list: {example_list_no_even}\")\n    try:\n        difference = diff_even_odd(example_list_no_even)\n        print(f\"Difference (first_even - first_odd): {difference}\")\n    except LookupError as e:\n        print(f\"Error: {e}\") # Expected: No even integer found\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```"}
