{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "```python\ndef validate_radius(radius: float | int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates and classifies the radius, raising TypeError for non-numeric input.\n    Returns 'negative', 'zero', or 'positive' based on the radius value.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(radius, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Radius must be a numeric value (int or float).\")\n    if radius < 0:\n        return 'negative'\n    elif radius == 0:\n        return 'zero'\n    else: # radius > 0\n        return 'positive'\n\ndef compute_area(radius: float | int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the area using the formula area = R^2.\n    Returns the computed area as a float.\n    \"\"\"\n    return float(radius * radius)\n\ndef triangle_area(radius: float | int) -> float | int | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the area of the largest triangle inscribed in a semicircle.\n    Handles negative, zero, and positive radii as per specification.\n    \"\"\"\n    classification = validate_radius(radius)\n\n    if classification == 'negative':\n        return None\n    elif classification == 'zero':\n        return 0\n    else: # classification == 'positive'\n        return compute_area(radius)\n```"}
