{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef _binary_search_right(arr: List[int], value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Internal helper returning insertion index using binary search semantics.\n    It finds the index where value can be inserted to maintain sorted order,\n    placing it after any existing equal elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] <= value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low\n\ndef right_insertion(arr: List[int], value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return right-biased insertion index for value into sorted arr.\n    Preconditions: arr is sorted in non-decreasing order (caller responsibility per SRS BR1).\n    Does not modify arr (no in-place mutation).\n    \"\"\"\n    return _binary_search_right(arr, value)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def _binary_right_insertion(seq, value) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Locates the lowest index where seq[index] > value, using binary search.\n    If no such index exists, returns len(seq).\"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(seq) - 1\n    ans = len(seq)  # Default: value is greater than all elements\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if seq[mid] > value:\n            ans = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        else:  # seq[mid] <= value, so look to the right\n            low = mid + 1\n    return ans\n\n\ndef right_insertion(seq, value) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return insertion index for value in ascending seq, inserting to the right of equals.\n    The returned index is in [0, len(seq)].\"\"\"\n    if len(seq) == 0:\n        return 0\n    return _binary_right_insertion(seq, value)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/787", "solution": "```python\n# src/__init__.py\n# This file marks the 'src' directory as a Python package.\n\n```\n```python\n# src/domain.py\nclass TextInput:\n    \"\"\"Holds input string and its length.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: str):\n        self.value: str = value\n        self.length: int = len(value)\n\nclass MatchPattern:\n    \"\"\"Holds the literal pattern \"abbb\".\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.pattern: str = \"abbb\"\n\nclass MatchResult:\n    \"\"\"Holds the boolean outcome of a match operation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, matched: bool):\n        self.matched: bool = matched\n\n```\n```python\n# src/text_match_three.py\nfrom src.domain import TextInput, MatchPattern, MatchResult\n\ndef text_match_three(text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the input string contains the contiguous substring \"abbb\".\n    Returns True if found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    text_input = TextInput(text)\n    match_pattern = MatchPattern()\n\n    # Short inputs cannot contain the pattern \"abbb\".\n    if text_input.length < len(match_pattern.pattern):\n        match_result = MatchResult(matched=False)\n    else:\n        # Scan the input string for the literal contiguous pattern.\n        found = match_pattern.pattern in text_input.value\n        match_result = MatchResult(matched=found)\n    \n    return match_result.matched\n\n```"}
