{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "```python\n# last-function/src/last_function.py\n\ndef last(lst: list, target: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the zero-based index of the last (rightmost) occurrence of target in a sorted list.\n    Returns -1 if the target is not found; assumes `lst` is sorted ascending.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(lst) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if lst[mid] == target:\n            result = mid  # Found a potential last occurrence\n            low = mid + 1 # Try to find an even later one in the right half\n        elif lst[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # lst[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\n```\n```python\n# last-function/tests/test_last.py\n\nfrom src.last_function import last\n\ndef test_last_example() -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests the last function with the specified acceptance test case.\n    Asserts that last([1,2,3], 1) correctly returns 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert last([1,2,3], 1) == 0\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "```python\n# src/last.py\n\"\"\"\nImplementation of last(list, target) as required by SRS.\nReturns: int index of last occurrence when found, or -1 when not found.\n\"\"\"\ndef last(list, target):\n    \"\"\"Return zero-based index of the last occurrence of target in list.\n    Returns: int index of last occurrence when found, or -1 when not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    left = 0\n    right = len(list) - 1\n    result = -1\n    while left <= right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if list[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            left = mid + 1\n        elif list[mid] < target:\n            left = mid + 1\n        else: # list[mid] > target\n            right = mid - 1\n    return result\n\n```\n```python\n# tests/test_last.py\nfrom src.last import last\n\n# Example acceptance test from SRS\nassert last([1,2,3],1) == 0\n\n# Optional wrapper\ndef test_example():\n    \"\"\"Verify the example acceptance test from the SRS.\"\"\"\n    assert last([1,2,3],1) == 0\n\n```"}
